            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0283" n="157" xml:id="pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89France/132: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-23T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23, 1925—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>235. Your 336, June 18, 6 p.m. Reference your first paragraph. I would be glad if
                    you can find it possible to suggest that in speech on July 3 intention be
                    publicly announced of sending commission to Washington to enter upon
                    debt-funding negotiations, and that an early date be set for commission’s
                    departure.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
